<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamburg America Line</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1847">1847</a>–<a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as HAPAG, Hamburg-Amerikanische Packetfahrt-Actien-Gesellschaft</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> America Line (HAPAG) was a shipping company founded in Hamburg in 1847 to carry passengers and mail across the Atlantic. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-ballin">Albert Ballin</a> it became the largest shipping company in the world by 1914, carrying millions of emigrants to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. It merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norddeutscher-lloyd">Norddeutscher Lloyd</a> in 1970 to form Hapag-Lloyd.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamburg-america-line.jpg" alt="Hamburg America Line" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HAPAG_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
